Legend:
* FlowerVariationOds data: denotes what the section is defining; think of it as the subsection title
* int id (first one): flower variation internal ID number (several got tangled with theme names as I was annotating, just ignore those)
* int flowerId: plant species internal ID number
* FlowerColor color: "what color the variation is"
* Int8 color: 1-9 (mostly) for solid colors, 10+ for hybrids
* Int8 isSpecial: if solid, isSpecial=0, if hybrid, isSpecial=1; if = 1, int8 color=internal hybrid color ID
* int probability: related to the color's chance to grow from seed? hybrids are all 0
* HW hash (originally "LocalizationHash languageHash"), SInt64 longHash, int intHash: hash codes for the variation's hedgehog words (see GameData.txt)
* int receivePrice: how many gold petals to receive it on a gift hedgehog
* ArrangementPoint arrangementPoints Array array int size = 124: "the next 124 sub-sub-subsections are how many points it'll score in Coordinate" 
* "[0] int id = 1" to "[116] (originally 123, broken in annotation) int id = 735": Coordinate ArrangementPoints; generally 1-100, actual base points will be a multiple of this number
* eventIds array int size = [number]: how many special events this plant is released during
* int id (after eventIds if int size=1 or more): ID numbers of the event it's released for. Includes both new standard releases (5012=released on May 1 2026) and anniversary ribbon/crown releases; see gamedata.txt

